            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Asparagus declinatus, common name bridal veil, is a species of Asparagus plant. It is native to the Cape Provinces, Madagascar and Namibia and has been introduced into Central America, South Australia and Western Australia. It is a perennial vine. It is categorized as invasive in some areas."
